Clamp the table indices in lut_interp_linear_float().

lut_interp_linear_float() (gfx/qcms/src/transform_util.rs) indexes its table with ceil() and
floor() of value * (len - 1), which is only in range for values in [0, 1]. The modular transform
chain does not guarantee that: transforming from the XYZ D50 identity profile
(Profile::new_XYZD50(), as the fuzz target does) to fuzz/samples/0316-eb3f97ab646cd7b66bee80bdfe6098ac.icc
passes a value of about -0.009, the negative index wraps when cast to usize, and
qcms_transform_create() panics with an index out of bounds. Clamp both indices to the table;
negative values already saturate to 0 in the float-to-usize cast.
Not fixed upstream as of mozilla-firefox b8cbe7118 (2026-11-21) or FirefoxGraphics/qcms
2ee13006ac (main, 2025-03-05).

Includes a test in src/gtest.rs (sample_0316_from_xyz) that runs that transform and a unit test
in src/transform_util.rs; both fail without the fix.

Upstream: none found.

